{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MJ-AgentLab/mj-agentlab-marketplace/pulls/284","id":4930518173,"node_id":"PR_kwDORoMukM8AAAABJeG8nQ","html_url":"https://github.com/MJ-AgentLab/mj-agentlab-marketplace/pull/284","diff_url":"https://github.com/MJ-AgentLab/mj-agentlab-marketplace/pull/284.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/MJ-AgentLab/mj-agentlab-marketplace/pull/284.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MJ-AgentLab/mj-agentlab-marketplace/issues/284","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MJ-AgentLab/mj-agentlab-marketplace/pulls/284/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MJ-AgentLab/mj-agentlab-marketplace/pulls/284/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MJ-AgentLab/mj-agentlab-marketplace/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MJ-AgentLab/mj-agentlab-marketplace/issues/284/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MJ-AgentLab/mj-agentlab-marketplace/statuses/318db5a5660920f4fcd95f0f96c352d012514815","number":284,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"fix(release): release 8.3.3 with HTML 0.1.38 repairs","user":{"login":"ranzuozhou","id":35538471,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NTM4NDcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35538471?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ranzuozhou","html_url":"https://github.com/ranzuozhou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ranzuozhou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ranzuozhou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ranzuozhou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ranzuozhou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ranzuozhou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ranzuozhou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ranzuozhou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ranzuozhou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ranzuozhou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Release v8.3.3 — HTML 0.1.38 repair\n\nHTML 0.1.37 generated artifacts omitted distributable asset notices and had a faint blank reflection boundary. This release carries scoped LICENSE/Apache notices, rejects portable output-name collisions before writing, checks installed LICENSE bytes and makes the control boundary visible. The release also carries PR281's bounded Linux browser-startup stderr diagnostics and the intervening synchronization/maintenance records. Guide and the other four plugin trees keep their runtime identities.\n\nThis is the release PR under #274, targeting protected `main` from complete actual-develop ancestry (PR283 merge `a4892f51f4163fb5bd4457d99229eaf1a4683e8f`, tree `196daab879d38b649333a01c4c0d0194c7b107c7`). Preparation base is main `e3dc40f734fc972e05956da3e908091e09963675`; public v8.3.2 remains tag/Release `f906b1001a86d7b5415451bd973bea26e6cc3a1d`. VERSION/badge are already 8.3.3; this PR does not bump again. Five packages/eight public skills/five explicit entries remain.\n\nRelease head: `318db5a5660920f4fcd95f0f96c352d012514815` / tree `44893ef4e8dcdc437d8bbeafb3b67960ef8baa29`. The independent staged-blob review passed before commit.\n\n### Verification\n\n- Actual283 full local run: 647 total, 646 PASS, zero FAIL and one platform-specific skip. Strict validation and exact CLI 0.147.0 passed.\n- Fresh actual283 installation, UTC02:56:38.655–03:09:46.916: 13 scenarios/178 commands all exit0; 6 Diagram and 18 Learning Evidence real Python calls; 4 generated artifacts and 4 static checks, each95/95. Runtime/cache and license bytes matched; all14 unique owned roots were removed and all state guards passed. This is separate from the earlier395 CI and original908 guard FAIL.\n- Release documentation candidate: 116/116 documentation/INTENT tests, strict validation and exact CLI baseline passed. 2,079 source bindings include the unchanged original1,890; the32-row accepted baseline retains its first five columns. Staged Git blobs receive an independent final closure check before commit.\n- The same owner-private Site v2 was deployed successfully from source `3d3082ff8cfa99576bbda816a3ecc3b0b787636d`; owner/custom policy revision1 and audience remained unchanged. Local Chrome155 QA covers320/390/1366 and control screenshots. Hosted full interaction/native matrices were not rerun; local input and native archive descriptors are explicitly distinct in the ledger.\n- New release-head server CI, latest base, resolved threads and real non-author/latest-pusher-external approval remain separate gates. AI review does not substitute for GitHub approval; no bypass is authorized.\n\n### Scope, authorization and retained limits\n\nOriginal B1/P5 and the five-boundary authorization cover this one repair release and the same private Site repair; the independent scope audit is linked in the [release ledger](docs/runbook/[RUNBOOK]_Marketplace_8_3_3_Release_Readiness.md). No new Owner decision is needed for these authorized technical steps.\n\nThe original core acceptance is ACCEPTED_LIMITED and does not accept this new0.1.38/Site v2 or the full plan. Native pending-window lifecycle, native dispatch, the second true client, remaining accessibility/hosted coverage and unmeasured learning effects remain open. Earlier startup/checkout/guard FAIL, UNKNOWN root cause, actual bypass and empty reviews/approval NOT_MET remain recorded. #274 stays open.\n\n### Publication and recovery\n\nMerge only after ordinary protected-main gates pass. VERSION on main invokes the existing draft-first release controls; actual main/tag/Release/run/notes/assets and fresh real-tag installation must then be independently verified. The default install ref stays real v8.3.2 until actual v8.3.3 exists. Stop on failed gates, identity/audience errors, unexpected material or uncertain results. Preserve v8.3.2 and private Site v1; recover with a bounded forward repair or protected new-version repair without rewriting old tags/Release assets.\n\n### Review checklist\n\n- [x] CHANGELOG has an empty Unreleased and complete8.3.3 section;8.3.2 and older Git bytes are preserved.\n- [x] Prepared VERSION/badge, exact five-package manifests and installation expectations agree; no second bump.\n- [x] Applicable bounded actual checks, isolated installation/Python, independent review,32 baseline rows and source closure are recorded.\n- [x] Root AGENTS/A6, canonical guide/spec, task INDEX/unique PLAN/REPORT and release ledger are synchronized;20 repository skills retain their contracts.\n- [x] Existing original conditional release authorization is reused; deferrals and old approval gaps are preserved without claiming full plan completion.\n- [ ] Current release-head CI, real independent approval, threads and latest main base all satisfy protection before merge.\n- [x] No new runtime/debug code beyond the inherited approved repairs; no credentials, unknown-rights research raw or old release overwrites.\n\n[Task entry](plans/274-html-learning-artifact/INDEX.md) · [Accepted baseline](plans/274-html-learning-artifact/[PLAN]_HTML_Learning_Artifact.md#accepted-baseline-and-authorization) · [Unique REPORT](plans/274-html-learning-artifact/[REPORT]_HTML_Learning_Artifact.md#actual283-and-repair-release-continuation) · [INT-2026-003](docs/intent/[INTENT]_INT-2026-003_HTML_Learning_Artifact.md)\n\nRefs #274\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-20T03:20:26Z","updated_at":"2026-10-20T03:20:26Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"ac34c52c0eab22368e5e2737ee59241f5aad2912","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"MJ-AgentLab:codex/release-html-learning-8-3-3","ref":"codex/release-html-learning-8-3-3","repo":{"id":1183002256,"node_id":"R_kgDORoMukA","name":"mj-agentlab-marketplace","full_name":"MJ-AgentLab/mj-agentlab-market